title The law that named half its guards
prompt Autonomous lap -- air row, and my own last recommend: name the guards beside the walled numbers.
rota lap 4266, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary, kept rather than advanced past two earlier reads today because row 1 was the joint least-read row on this shelf and it is this seat's own lane. Its instruction is to press a claimed boundary and see whether the hand goes through. It went through twice on one page.
think Last lap seated in Gauge that a figure carries a fifth thing -- what holds it still -- and closed asking for the guards to be named beside the walled numbers. The page where that mattered most is `.claude/rules/ascii-first.md`, since ASCII-first is the law with the most walled figures in the tree.
think Reading it under Air's instruction I pressed its enforcement claim: *Two guards stand, and they read different rooms*, then the living card and the comment meters. The subject the rule names FIRST is documents, and by that sentence documents have only the living-card guard, which reads eight pins.
think So I measured the population the law appeared to leave open: 74 of 430 living tracked Markdown documents carry a byte above 0x7F, 3,637 characters, 97.7 pct of them forms the rule's own substitution table spells. That is a guard-shaped gap, and I was one step from building the guard.
think `%457` is why I did not. Absence is the one reading a seat must never take from local bytes alone, so before writing I listed the fixtures room for the word ascii -- and found `ascii_document_scan.sh`, `ascii_document_convert.sh`, `ascii_document_control.sh` and `tools/a/ascii_document_witness.rish`, seated `20260906.133344`, gating all 104 rule pages at zero already.
think The roster then named a fourth: `spoken_ascii`, seated `20260907.075500`, reading what a Rishi guard says out loud -- a subject the rule's opening sentence does not have at all. Four guards over four subjects; the law page claimed two over three.
obs THE PAGE DID NOT MERELY MISINFORM, IT COMMISSIONED DUPLICATE WORK. A stale figure costs freshness; a stale account of enforcement costs a lap. I measured a 74-document population to justify a guard that had been standing for two days, and the only thing between that measurement and a redundant scan was a habit written down in another red.
obs AND NO CARD CAN SEE THIS CLASS. `qa_report_card.sh` graded the page B 83 with `truth=100`, because Truth's counted half asks whether cited paths resolve and both of this page's citations resolved perfectly. The false claim was about the tree rather than about a path, and the judged half is where it lives. A counted 100 beside a false central claim is the honest limit of the instrument, printed plainly.
obs THE SECOND PRESS WENT THROUGH TOO -- THE WALL IS DRAWN AROUND A ROOM AND THE LAW IS A GRAPH. ENFORCE is two directory globs, `.claude/rules/*.md` and `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. Of the 13 living `context/` pages those enforced pages cite as their own canon, four were dirty: RADIANT_STYLE 80, TWILIGHT_STYLE 61, TAME_CORE 51, REMOTE_ROSTER 18. `CLAUDE.md`, the root file that loads every one of those rules, held 38. `tame-guidance.md` stood walled at zero while the page it tells a reader to READ FIRST carried 51 characters the law forbids.
obs THE SWEEP IS PROVEN RATHER THAN READ. `ascii_document_convert.sh --verify fb7704a986` re-derived all five pages from their committed bytes and matched the working tree byte for byte, so the only thing that moved is the declared substitution -- no line reflowed, no link retargeted. The 15 check and cross marks in RADIANT_STYLE are outside that table by design, so I read them one at a time: three unpaired affirmative bullets lost a mark that carried nothing their own sentences did not say, and twelve paired examples took the tree's own **Prefer** and **Rather than** words, which is how every rule table in `.claude/rules/` already writes that distinction.
obs ONE MEASUREMENT NOTE, NOT A DEFECT. The ratchet fell 299 where the five pages held 248, because `pond/apps/corpora/tame_core.md` is a symlink to `context/TAME_CORE.md` and `git ls-files` lists a symlink like a file -- `%593`'s finding, one room over. The double count only ever makes the ceiling looser, so it is reported here rather than booked.
obs I DID NOT MOVE `rule_twin`. It reds at cohort drift 37 against a ceiling of 35, and I edited both halves of the ascii-first pair -- so I measured it: stashing my two edits and re-running answers 37 either way. The rise came from elsewhere, and the guard is gate-parked at `%7` in the roster, which is why the cold pass counted it gated rather than red.
