scope one Air lap -- the ASCII law's account of its own enforcement made true, its canon pages swept to zero, the ratchet lowered to meet them, and one red closed on the shared shelf
status GREEN on the round's own work, with one condition named. Hot pass over the staged tree: 186 guards, 1370s, 177 green, 3 gated (`rule_twin` at `%7`, both `pond_enclosure_*` at `%5`), 6 red and every one closed or accounted. `fold_shelf_link` and `fold_shelf_link_repoint` read the two depth-lost links my own new shelf carried -- the elder card block quotes `archive/...` paths relative to `construction/`, and copying it verbatim into `construction/archive/` cost them a directory; `fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh` corrected both and the scan reads `fold_depth_lost=0`. `reds_ledger_headline` regenerated to 610/590/610 and GREEN. `reds_ledger_monotone` and `reds_row_present` read `expected row 611, found 612`: I booked from the anointed spine as `derived-spine` requires and this checkout has yet to rebase, so row 611 exists upstream and not here -- the gap closes on the rebase this send takes, and it is re-verified there rather than claimed here. `standing_equipment` reds while any member does. `rule_twin` reds at cohort drift 37 over 35 and is not mine: stashing my two ascii-first edits and re-running answers 37 either way.
status_reverify The rebase onto `xy/main` took four upstream commits and conflicted on `construction/REDS.md`: upstream had booked `%611` while this round folded `%604`, `%607` and `%608` away, so the resolution kept both new rows and the fold. A SECOND rebase then found upstream had published its own `%612` at `20260908.052546` -- four seconds before mine -- and had folded `%604` and `%607` itself, so this row renumbered by the earlier-stamp rule and re-folded only `%608`. A THIRD rebase found `%614` and `%615` published too, and it landed at `%616`. Each move cost one line: every living citation already spelled the stamp, which is what `derived-spine` rule 4 is for. `index_row_bound` then read one misordered row on the shared day shelf -- the `%440` shape, a rebase auto-merging a peer's row, repaired again by `index_shelf_repair.sh`. Full re-verify over the staged tree afterward: **187 guards, 1478s, 183 green, 3 gated, 1 red -- `standing_equipment` alone**, on its own control leg `live_group_plant`, which this pen cannot build and which `%549`'s row already names. Every member guard green, `reds_ledger_monotone`, `reds_row_present`, `fold_shelf_link` and `fold_shelf_link_repoint` among them.
recommend keep-going -- the ENFORCE roster is the open half: widening it from two directory globs to the canon those globs NAME is a small derived change to `ascii_document_scan.sh`, and the population it would gate now stands at zero, so the wall can be raised on a tree already clean.
